__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.var/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Local orchestrator profile (self-hosting); machine-specific, keep untracked like job-cannon
orchestrator.config.yaml

# Agent/tool scratch output (nit-pick-supreme, devin CLI, ad-hoc session work).
# NB: scripts/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the fleet launcher lives there and
# is load-bearing (see scripts/fleet-pass-hidden.vbs).
scratchpad/
.nit-supreme/
.devin/

# Host-local operational logs and one-off artifacts
proc-monitor.log
rollcall_charlie.json
*.tmp_log*.txt
test_marker*.txt
*.bak
# MSYS/Cygwin crash dumps. Written to the repo root by whatever cwd bash died in,
# so they land untracked and `git add .` will happily commit one.
*.stackdump

# Worker/orchestrator protocol residue written into the worktree root at runtime.
# These are state sentinels, not source: a worker writes them per-session and
# salvage/reap tooling reads them back. If tracked, a fresh worktree materializes
# a phantom outcome before the worker has done anything, and a worker's own write
# shows up as a modification to a tracked file -- the exact shape of dirt that
# trips the worktree_unsafe escalation path (issue #1138). Ignoring them here is
# structural prevention so neither workers' own writes nor a salvage that
# `git add -A`s a worktree with residue can commit them again.
.worker-outcome.json
.charlie-writer.json
# Worker PR-body scratch files. The worker prompt does not name a file, but
# workers ad-hoc draft their PR body into a PR_BODY_<issue>.md file in the
# worktree root before passing it to `gh pr create --body`. Salvage squash
# #1197 committed PR_BODY_1010.md to main this way (issue #1204). The glob
# closes the class: any issue number, present or future, is covered.
PR_BODY_*.md
# The remaining variants mirror worktree.py's _LAUNCHER_OWNED_PR_BODY_RE
# (issue #1391), which the dirty-check already recognizes but .gitignore did
# not -- so a `_pr_body.md` (issue #1541 rework) or `.pr_body_<issue>.md`
# (issue #1418) scratch file slipped past `git add` and got committed. These
# globs close the same class at the ignore layer so the ad-hoc spellings the
# regex already governs cannot recur via `git add`.
_pr_body*.md
.pr_body*.md
.worker-pr-body*.md

# Session planning/handoff documents are machine-local working notes, often
# containing host paths and operational detail that must not ship in the
# public tree. Anything meant to be published belongs in docs/ proper, not
# docs/plans/. (A few legacy files remain tracked; the rule prevents new ones
# from being swept in by a broad `git add`.)
docs/plans/
# Ad-hoc acceptance-check probe scripts from observation-window sessions.
scripts/ac3_*.py
